WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:02.310
December 2015.

2
00:00:02.360 --> 00:00:04.830
Storm Desmond brought
rain records to Cumbria,

3
00:00:04.880 --> 00:00:09.370
and gusts up to about
130 kilometres per hour.

4
00:00:09.420 --> 00:00:13.330
The Met Office issues forecast
charts up to five days ahead,

5
00:00:13.380 --> 00:00:15.710
updated about every 12 hours.

6
00:00:15.760 --> 00:00:20.350
On each chart: an H, an
L, and a few curved lines.

7
00:00:20.400 --> 00:00:22.670
Do the lines show where it will rain?

8
00:00:22.720 --> 00:00:24.350
Is it just experience?

9
00:00:24.400 --> 00:00:27.630
How can a few curved lines warn of a gale?

10
00:00:27.680 --> 00:00:31.070
In this mission, you'll learn
to read a synoptic chart:

11
00:00:31.120 --> 00:00:34.310
its lines, its letters and its symbols.

12
00:00:34.360 --> 00:00:37.570
Then you'll read satellite
images, by day and by night,

13
00:00:37.620 --> 00:00:40.050
and check them against the chart.

14
00:00:40.100 --> 00:00:45.210
Your mission: find out how forecasters
spot a coming gale from a few curved lines

15
00:00:45.260 --> 00:00:46.110
on a map.
